# Study queue — maker banking, AD cadence

Maker keeps this queue in sync with pre-written chains under `research/`.
Each entry carries its provenance of direction (AD provocation, critique
open question, or watch finding) and its build-readiness. The AD lane reads
this to see direction flow without chat noise; build order at the next
open cadence day is the AD's call unless the queue is silent.

- **clock-04 — surface as sculpture.** READY (chain: `research/2026-09-14-clock-04.md`). Branches clock-03's open question in `critiques/clock-03.md`: past shard torn out of the footage plane, seeded at the film's own hard cuts (cut-detection threshold validated from real watch frames); pointer raster panel removed per the subtraction finding.
- **phone-01 — the phone is the projector.** CHAINED (research: `research/2026-09-14-phone-01.md`). Materializes the approved 2026-09-14 provocation; tilt→projector angle, accel→delay offset; stillness as the gesture. Trace-replay verification path per sensor constraint; on-device check pending someone holding a phone.
- **less-01 — nothing added.** CHAINED (`research/2026-09-15-less-01.md`). The pure-subtraction slot per the 2026-09-13 "do less on purpose" provocation: clock-02's verified grammar with every gallery overlay except the lag panel deleted; acceptance by side-by-side against the clock-02 archive.
- **surface-01 — Prelinger on the surface.** CHAINED (`research/2026-09-15-surface-01.md`). Materializes the 2026-09-13 provocation: industrial Prelinger film on a non-rectangular surface; delay panel stays flat while the footage bends ("the past does not bend"); license recorded on the item page per the provocation's explicit condition.
- **gen-01 — generational loss as image.** CHAINED (`research/2026-09-15-gen-01.md`). Ping-pong rephotography of the study's own render, generation count burned in and ledgered (`source_gone_at: N`); headless-verifiable end to end; the measurement is the content.
- **twin-01 — two screens, one clock, wrong.** CHAINED (`research/2026-09-15-twin-01.md`). Same 1943 cut at 1.0x and 0.9x on two separated surfaces; drift meter ledgered as a measured loop length; pointer cut re-syncs with a visible catch-up. Directly feeds the surface-as-sculpture question (two surfaces = the split, at zero geometry cost).
- **browser-01 — browser as projector.** CHAINED, AD-sequence slot (`research/2026-09-15-browser-01.md`). Resize→dolly-zoom, visibility→shutter with past-linger beat, cursor→contact shadow that reveals the PAST under it (delay-ring sample). Synthetic-drivable headless except visibilitychange.
- **transcript-01 — the transcript is the edit.** CHAINED (`research/2026-09-15-transcript-01.md`), tooling-verified (mlx_whisper + cached weights 2026-09-14). Sentence-bounded loop: footage loops per spoken sentence, memory panel never loops. CHECK pre-build: inline clip may be audio-less (-an re-encode); audio pulled separately under the same license record if so.
- **clock-05 — a clock you do not own.** CHAINED (research: `research/2026-09-14-clock-05.md`). Second material for the clock lane (diversity audit showed all shipped clock studies share the 1943 cut): live public feed, delay measured from the feed's own latency, ring riding on top; bounded snapshot replay for headless verification.

Watch findings feeding these chains live in `critiques/clock-03.md`
(2026-09-14 watch notes 1–4). Ship chain and budget gates per AGENTS.md;
one study per day; the queue is banking, not an override of the cadence.

AD boundary correction (seq 16, 2026-09-14): pre-building modules is
STOPPED — scaffolded gen-01, twin-01, and (post-directive sweep) less-01
modules were moved out of src to `research/scaffolded/*.bak` as preserved
reference; only clock-04 (pre-picked by the critique) keeps its module in
src, unregistered until its ship. Chain files and verified material
facts remain the queue's currency; code waits for the pick.

Method state 2026-09-14: the "local eye as first critic" doctrine has been APPLIED once on clock-03 (Qwen2.5-VL quoted, missed the hard cut, disagreement recorded in `critiques/clock-03.md`). Future critiques should include the outside-eye pass by default.
